## Context

The author: « les canaux structurés laggent 1-3 ans et l'enjeu en M2 M3 AEDIST [numbering from before 2026-09-29; 1185 belongs to M3a]
est justement de mieux suivre en quasi temps réel » [structured channels lag
1-3 years and the stake in M2 M3 AEDIST is precisely to track more closely in
near real time]. The source to prefer is the primary publication closest to
the event, dated by its own collection (for example the ADB project sheet,
"Last PDS Update"). CRS and IATI serve for reconciliation and catch-up. The
IATI lag depends on the publisher and is not known for ADB: it is measured, not
assumed.

## Actions

1. On the ADB projects of the [[1183]] pilot (56140-001, 56368-001), record,
   for a few dated facts (approval, signing, entry into force, first
   disbursements), the date at which each appears in the primary source, in
   IATI and in CRS.
2. Extend to one or two other donors present in the register if access allows.
3. Write the measurement up as a methods note, with figures tied to archived
   outputs.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] For each recorded fact, the three dates (or "absent on day D") are traced to an archived file
- [ ] The lag is reported by channel and by donor, with its uncertainty, without extrapolation beyond the measured cases
- [ ] The note says which primary source to prefer for each type of fact
